    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Assistant-Director--Residence-Life--69-E-_JR100248": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Residence Life (69-E)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-19\nPosted: Posted 16 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Director, Residence Life (69-E) ‌ Position Type: Regular ‌ About the Role: The Assistant Director of Residence Life provides leadership, supervision, and strategic direction for residential education and student engagement within University Housing. This live-on professional oversees Residence Hall Directors, student leadership structures, and key residential processes that support student success, community development, and well-being. The role includes operational oversight, staff development, crisis response, student conduct administration, and collaboration with campus partners to enhance the residential experience. ‌ Essential Duties and Responsibilities Staff Supervision & Leadership Provide direct supervision, coaching, and evaluation for all Residence Hall Directors (RHDs) Conduct formal evaluations and provide ongoing feedback and professional development for entry-level staff Serve as a member of the departmental Leadership Team (LT) Participate in the LT On-Call rotation for crisis and after-hours response Serve as a member of the Professional Staff Recruitment Committee, when applicable Student Leadership & Engagement Oversee Residence Hall Association (RHA) and student leadership initiatives Serve as RHA Advisor and provide oversight of Community Councils Support student leadership development through training, advising, and strategic planning Resident Assistant Program Chair the RA Recruitment, Selection, and Placement Committee Chair the RA Training and Development Committee Manage the KCE Model of Programming and community engagement efforts Support ongoing development and assessment of the Resident Assistant program Student Support & Community Standards Serve as the first point of contact for elevated parental/guardian concerns Manage higher-level student conduct cases in collaboration with departmental and institutional policies Provide oversight of the roommate agreement process Conduct academic grade checks and facilitate academic success conversations with Resident Assistants Participate on the CARE Team, as available and when permitted Operations & Administrative Oversight Manage and oversee departmental Resident Assistant Resource Rooms Ensure implementation of residential education practices that support student success and community development Support departmental initiatives, assessment, and strategic priorities Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s Degree, plus two years of Residence Life, University Housing, or Student Affairs/Development experience Demonstrated experience supervising staff or student leaders Experience with student conduct processes, crisis response, or case management Strong interpersonal, organizational, and conflict resolution skills Ability to respond to after-hours responsibilities Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree in Higher Education, Student Affairs, Counseling, or a related field Experience supervising professional live-in staff Experience advising student leadership organizations Experience designing or implementing training programs Familiarity with residential curriculum or educational programming models Experience working with academic success initiatives or student retention efforts Work Environment & Expectations Possible live-on position with housing provided based on salary allocation Participation in on-call rotation and crisis response Evening and weekend work required based on departmental needs Application Information Applicants should submit a resume, cover letter, and contact information for professional references. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. ‌ Posted Salary: ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands:"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Director-of-Development_JR100306": {
      "title": "Director of Development",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-19\nPosted: Posted 16 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Director of Development ‌ Position Type: Regular ‌ About the Role: Northern Kentucky University seeks an experienced and dynamic fundraiser to secure major gifts that advance the key priorities of the College of Health and Human Services. Serving as a strategic partner to college leadership, this position will play a pivotal role in driving transformational progress and elevating philanthropic impact and across the college. ‌ The Director of Development’s primary responsibility is to secure philanthropic support by managing the donor cycle for a portfolio of major gift prospects and donors. Duties and Responsibilities: Serve as the lead development representative for the College of Health and Human Services, partnering with Dean Gannon Tagher and academic leadership to shape strategic fundraising plans and translate academic initiatives into compelling philanthropic opportunities. Build and steward meaningful relationships with donors and prospects by aligning their philanthropic interests with college priorities, partnering with Advancement colleagues and academic partners to deliver personalized engagement opportunities. Secure philanthropic commitments at the major gift level, achieving an overall fundraising goal of $1M+ annually. Discover new prospects with the capacity and inclination to make a major gift, working closely with Prospect Development on the identification process. Maintain accurate records of prospect and donor interactions and proposal activity using university systems, ensuring compliance with all reporting deadlines.  Support the strategic direction of University Advancement, collaborating across the division on special projects and assignments identified by leadership. Applicants must have a bachelor’s degree and three to five years of fundraising experience. The ideal candidate will have a background in higher education, a demonstrated track record of securing individual philanthropic gifts, and exceptional interpersonal skills with the ability to communicate effectively. This position reports to the Assistant Vice President of Development, University Advancement. ‌ Posted Salary: ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands:"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Coordinator--Career-Readiness-and-Employer-Partnerships_JR100384": {
      "title": "Coordinator, Career Readiness and Employer Partnerships",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Coordinator, Career Readiness and Employer Partnerships ‌ Position Type: Regular ‌ About the Role: The Coordinator, Career Readiness and Employer Partnerships is the primary liaison between the College of Arts & Sciences and the Norse Network Hub, connecting employers with faculty, staff, and students to expand career opportunities and strengthen employer partnerships. This position coordinates employer engagement activities, communicates opportunities across the College, and supports initiatives that align academic programs with workforce needs. ‌ Employer Engagement Serve as the College's primary contact for employer engagement activities with the Norse Network Hub. Connect employers with appropriate faculty, programs, and departments. Identify and communicate employer partnership opportunities that support student career development and experiential learning. Collaboration & Programming Coordinate employer events and engagement activities within the College, including information sessions, networking events, classroom presentations, and employer visits. Collaborate with faculty, Career Services, and Hub staff to expand employer involvement in student learning and career readiness initiatives. Foster strong relationships among employers, faculty, and academic leadership. Communication & Reporting Attend regular Hub meetings and share employer engagement updates. Track employer interactions and engagement activities using designated university systems. Support continuous improvement by sharing best practices and identifying opportunities to strengthen employer partnerships. Required Qualifications Bachelor's degree required. Excellent communication, organizational, and relationship-building skills. Ability to manage multiple priorities and collaborate effectively with internal and external stakeholders. Experience coordinating programs, events, or partnership initiatives. Preferred Qualifications Experience in higher education, employer relations, workforce development, career services, or community engagement. Familiarity with Handshake, TeamDynamix, or similar CRM/event management systems. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Strong interpersonal, communication, and networking skills. Project and event coordination experience. Ability to work independently while building collaborative partnerships. Commitment to student success and employer engagement. Please attach a resume, cover letter and references. ‌ Posted Salary: ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands:"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Peer-Support-Specialist_JR100264": {
      "title": "Peer Support Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nPart time\n\nPosition Title: Peer Support Specialist ‌ Position Type: Fixed Term (Fixed Term) ‌ About the Role: Assist peers in articulating recovery goals and learning/practicing new skills, supporting them in their treatment and advocating themselves for services. Share personal recovery stories to show that recovery is attainable. ‌ Serve as a mentor to clients to promote hope and personal empowerment .   Exemplify recovery principles for clients.   May   assist   with transportation, groups, behavioral health providers, MRT classes, or care coordinators and reentry specialists.   Mentor clients .   Coordinating client care .   Serving as   a healthcare   advocate for   clients .   KNOWLEDGE,   SKILLS   AND ABILITIES   (KSAs ): ​ Good data entry skills, ability to exercise discretion, and   maintain   confidentiality. Compliance with all HIPAA regulations and   adhere strictly   to confidentiality measures. ​   EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE:   ​ ​ High school diploma and 1 year of related experience.   ​ Must have passed Kentucky Adult Peer Support Specialist training and received Kentucky certification. ​   ‌ Posted Salary: ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands: A valid driver's license is required."
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Director-of-Financial-Services_JR100386": {
      "title": "Director of Financial Services",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Director of Financial Services ‌ Position Type: Regular ‌ About the Role: Northern Kentucky University seeks a collaborative and strategic financial leader to serve as the Director of Financial Services (University Accounting & Treasury Services). Reporting to the Associate Vice President for Financial Services, this position is responsible for overseeing the University's day-to-day accounting and treasury operations, including general accounting, financial reporting, treasury management, capital asset accounting, and accounts payable. The Director ensures the accuracy, integrity, and timeliness of the University's financial records and reporting while maintaining compliance with Generally Accepted Accounting Principles (GAAP), Governmental Accounting Standards Board (GASB) standards, and applicable federal and state regulations. This position plays a critical leadership role in the annual financial statement audit process, development of financial policies and procedures, implementation of accounting systems, and continuous improvement of business processes. The Director supervises accounting staff, partners closely with stakeholders across the institution, and serves as a key advisor and backup to the Associate Vice President for Financial Services. ‌ Primary Responsibilities Financial Leadership & Oversight Provide leadership and supervision for accounting and treasury services staff, including assigning work, establishing priorities, evaluating performance, and fostering professional development. Ensure the integrity and accuracy of the University's accounting records, financial transactions, and reporting processes. Review and approve journal entries, account reconciliations, and other accounting transactions to ensure compliance with University policies, GAAP, and GASB standards. Oversee the University's accounts payable operations, ensuring timely and accurate processing of payments and compliance with applicable policies and procedures. Financial Reporting & Compliance Lead the preparation of monthly, quarterly, and annual financial reports. Coordinate and prepare the University's annual financial statements and related disclosures. Manage year-end closing activities, including preparation of closing entries, reconciliations, and audit schedules. Serve as the primary liaison with external auditors and coordinate responses to audit requests. Monitor new GASB pronouncements and accounting requirements, assess institutional impact, and implement changes necessary to ensure compliance. Develop, maintain, and communicate accounting policies, procedures, and internal controls. Systems & Process Improvement Coordinate the development and enhancement of financial accounting and reporting systems. Partner with Information Technology, Human Resources, Student Financial Services, and other campus departments to support and improve integrated financial systems. Act as a subject matter expert for financial systems, including ERP and reporting tools. Identify opportunities to streamline processes, improve efficiency, strengthen internal controls, and enhance financial reporting capabilities. External Reporting Coordinate the preparation, review, and submission of required external reports, including but not limited to: FISAP IPEDS Council on Postsecondary Education (CPE) reporting Annual Comprehensive Financial Report (ACFR/CAFR) American Bar Association (ABA) reporting Management Information Reports (MIR) Other federal, state, and regulatory reporting requirements Review activity and financial information from affiliated entities, including foundations, when necessary for external reporting purposes. Strategic Support Provide financial expertise and guidance to University leadership. Lead or participate in special projects and strategic initiatives as assigned. Serve as backup to the Associate Vice President for Financial Services. Minimum Qualifications Master's degree in Accounting, Finance, Business Administration, or a closely related field. Minimum of seven (7) years of progressively responsible accounting, financial reporting, or treasury management experience. Demonstrated supervisory or management experience. Experience preparing audited financial statements and coordinating external audits. Strong knowledge of GAAP and GASB accounting standards. Preferred Qualifications Certified Public Accountant (CPA) strongly preferred. Experience in higher education, governmental, or nonprofit accounting. Experience with Workday, or similar enterprise financial systems. Experience preparing regulatory and compliance reports in a higher education environment. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Comprehensive knowledge of accounting principles, financial reporting, treasury operations, and internal controls. Strong understanding of GAAP, GASB, and governmental accounting practices. Exceptional analytical, organizational, and problem-solving skills. Ability to manage multiple priorities and deadlines in a complex environment. Strong written and verbal communication skills. Ability to build collaborative relationships across departments and stakeholders. Demonstrated leadership and team development skills. High level of accuracy, attention to detail, and commitment to compliance. Ability to maintain confidentiality and exercise sound professional judgment. Advanced proficiency in Microsoft Excel and working knowledge of Microsoft Office applications. Experience with Workday and financial reporting tools is preferred. Please attach a resume, cover letter and references. ‌ Posted Salary: ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands:"
    },
