    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Manager--Admin--Events---Special-Projects_JR100377": {
      "title": "Manager, Admin, Events & Special Projects",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Manager, Admin, Events & Special Projects ‌ Position Type: Regular ‌ About the Role: The Coordinator for Events and Special Projects is a highly organized role in the Office of the Provost who provides critical support to the Academic and Student Affairs division. The role ensures compliance with faculty credentialing requirements and accreditation standards, manages faculty data and reporting systems, and coordinates strategic events and recurring meetings hosted by the Provost’s Office. This position also serves as a liaison to academic and administrative units across the university, supporting the Vice Provost through effective communication, project tracking, and logistical coordination. By combining administrative expertise, event management, and data oversight, the position contributes to the efficiency, visibility, and reputation of the division. ‌ Serve as system administrator for Faculty Success, ensuring accurate collection and reporting of faculty teaching, research/creative activity, and service data. Manage faculty credentialing records required for accreditation, including transcripts, promotion/tenure data, and faculty status updates.  Maintain the Faculty Success website, granting system access as appropriate, collaborating with IT to enhance functionality, and ensuring course load and syllabus data are updated each term. Respond to current and former student syllabi requests. Plan and coordinate events and recurring programs hosted by the Office of the Provost, including Faculty & Staff Awards, First and Final Fridays, Faculty Development Awards, New Faculty/Administrator Orientation, GSE programming, fall Convocation Week, faculty appreciation events, special guest lectures and such. Oversee event logistics, including scheduling facilities, catering, RSVP tracking, seating, communications, and promotional materials. Coordinate official faculty portrait projects in collaboration with the library. Provide comprehensive administrative support to the Vice Provost, including coordinating travel arrangements, calendar management, processing expense reports, tracking, reconciling, and allocating monthly procurement card expenses, managing time approvals, and preparing meeting agendas and minutes. Support search committees by managing candidate travel and logistics Schedule bi-weekly, monthly, and semi-annual meetings between Risepoint and multiple internal and external university-wide stakeholders. Reserve rooms and arrange for technical support for on-campus meetings. Assist with preparing documentation, reports, presentations, and communications and reports for internal and external audiences, ensuring data accuracy. Bachelor’s Degree and three years of experience required.  Requires the ability to maintain confidentiality, exercise sound judgment, and demonstrate strong organizational and communication skills. Occasional flexibility in work hours may be necessary to support evening or weekend events. Please provide a resume, cover letter and references. ‌ Posted Salary: ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands:"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Part-time-faculty--College-of-Business_JR100075": {
      "title": "Part time faculty, College of Business",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPosition Title: Part time faculty, College of Business ‌ Position Type: Fixed Term (Fixed Term) ‌ About the Role: This is posting is to collect applications of those interested in teaching within the College of Business. ‌ The College of Business invites applications for inclusion in its part time faculty pool. The college seeks qualified professionals and educators who may be considered for part-time teaching assignments on an as-needed basis. Part time faculty provide instruction in support of the college's academic programs and are expected to create an engaging learning environment that promotes student success. Opportunities may be available across a variety of disciplines within the college, depending on departmental needs and course offerings. Submission of an application to this pool does not guarantee employment or an offer of assignment. Applications will be reviewed by academic departments as instructional needs arise. ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands:"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Faculty_JR100376": {
      "title": "Faculty",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Faculty ‌ Position Type: Regular ‌ About the Role: Tenure-track, Assistant Professor in VFX, Animation and Game Design, in the School of Media and Communication ‌ Assistant Professor position (tenure-track) in VFX, Animation and Game Design The School of Media and Communication at Northern Kentucky University seeks outstanding candidates with expertise in designing engaging interactive media for a tenure track Assistant Professor position, beginning in August 2027. The candidates are expected to excel in the classroom, be forward thinking in their creative and/or research agenda and enthusiastically engage with the public and university. They will embrace the opportunity to augment our faculty’s strengths in 3D content creation, game design and traditional media while shaping the evolution of our forays into interactive media, digital imaging, visual effects, and/or real time production for storytelling. This position is key to bridging creative and conceptual alliances with other units across campus and within our region. Successful candidates are expected to teach undergraduate courses in our 3D Digital Design and VFX (DFX) program (see Program Description and Full Catalog of Courses ), conduct an active creative and/or research program, and engage deeply with our students and region. As such, each candidate should be able to demonstrate teaching effectiveness, scholarship, and service related to the fast-changing world of media. A strong portfolio in peer-reviewed academic and/or creative work that demonstrates expertise in applying theory to practice in media creation is required. Applicable skill sets and academic focus will vary, but it is expected that applicants will be experienced in and passionate about visual effects, computer generated graphics, 3D modeling and animation, and/or real time production, and how these techniques affect visual storytelling and how we communicate. A Master’s degree in the emerging/immersive/digital media, informatics or other field directly related to media creation is required; an MFA or Ph.D. in such a field is preferred. A complete application will require: a letter of application, select examples of creative or scholarly work, CV, copies of recent teaching evaluations (qualitative and quantitative), and three letters of reference. Any candidate who is offered a position at NKU will be required to go through a pre-employment criminal background check as mandated by state law. Questions regarding the use of the website should be directed to the Human Resources Department at jobs@nku.edu . Questions regarding the nature of the position should be directed to the search committee chair, Dr. Stacie Jankowski at meihauss1@nku.edu . Review of applications will begin September 14, 2026 and continue until the position has been filled. Equal Opportunity Statement The University provides equal opportunities in educational services and employment according to law. ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands:"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Coordinator--Scheduling-Catalog_JR100372": {
      "title": "Coordinator, Scheduling/Catalog",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Coordinator, Scheduling/Catalog ‌ Position Type: Regular ‌ About the Role: To advance the focus on student success, this position will be responsible for coordination of class scheduling, booking rooms for courses, and university-wide events within SAP and Ad Astra (room scheduling software). This position is responsible for the creation and maintenance of the University's undergraduate catalog that is published annually. Collaboration with academic and administrative departments across the university is vital. This position will assist the Assistant Registrar of Systems, as well as any additional duties assigned by Office of the University Registrar administration. ‌ Course section maintenance in SAP and Ad Astra:  Enters and updates Course Sections in SAP and Ad Astra submitted through Event Planning Add/Change/Cancel forms daily.  Assigns classroom space to sections. Assist academic departments with issues in entering section through the event planning applications. Disperses communication throughout campus community in regards to schedule building and items that require action. Conducts training sessions for new personnel across the campus that will be working within Event Planning   Event Scheduling: Approves classroom space for non academic events through Ad Astra. Maintains rooms and buildings contained within SAP and Astra. Resolves conflicts with events   Reporting: Runs timely reports from SAP and Ad Astra to ensure that classrooms are assigned to sections and for conflict free room assignments for events. Also provide reports to evaluate room utilization, potential conflicts, and provide meaningful analytics. Utilizes Crystal Reports to provide detailed and customized reports for data within Ad Astra. Reviews reports and surveys cycles of class/event scheduling to continually streamline and simplify processes.  Perform optimization runs as required.   Catalog Coordination and Publication:  Serves as the primary catalog coordinator at the undergraduate level.  Reviews content for accuracy from university departments. Reviews content for accuracy and facilitates the collaboration with the pertinent university departments and offices;  monitors the curricular process; provides support to users of the online catalog.   Serves as the final approver and editor for every proposed change in the catalog’s database. Publishes the catalog as required (typically annually).  Position requires: Bachelors degree and 2 years of related experience Ability to easily navigate and utilize the Microsoft Office Suite. Experience with SAP and relevant work within collegiate studies is preferred, as well as experience with reporting tools. Must have strong attention to detail.   Previous experience with training or public speaking is preferred, while strong communication skills are required.   Good customer rapport skills needed. Please attach a resume, cover letter and references. ‌ Posted Salary: ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands:"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Fully-Remote/Stream-Restoration-Construction-Manager_JR100354-1": {
      "title": "Stream Restoration Construction Manager",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Stream Restoration Construction Manager ‌ Position Type: Fixed Term (Fixed Term) ‌ About the Role: The Stream Restoration Construction Manager conducts construction, training, supervises junior staff and interns, and performs other tasks for stream mitigation projects under supervision of the CER Director. This position will be based in Maysville and Carlisle ‌ 1. Conduct stream restoration construction, including surveying/stakeout, earth moving equipment operation, tree removal, sediment and erosion control, etc. Train and supervise junior staff and interns in these tasks. Oversee contractors. 2. Conduct other conservation and related tasks such as assessments, access road construction, invasive plant eradication, native planting, refuse removal, etc. Train and supervise junior staff and interns in these tasks. 3. Assemble and maintain field vehicles, tools, equipment, etc. Update and implement health and safety practices and training. Assist in recruiting and onboarding junior staff and interns. Train and supervise junior staff and interns in these tasks. ‌ Posted Salary: ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands:"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Admissions-Counselor_JR100320": {
      "title": "Admissions Counselor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Admissions Counselor ‌ Position Type: Regular ‌ About the Role: Admissions counselors will manage an assigned recruitment territory that requires developing and maintaining contacts with school counselors, organizations, agencies and clubs for the purposes of recruiting students. Counselors will travel frequently within and outside of normal business hours to represent the university at recruitment events and activities. Counselors will counsel students and parents about postsecondary educational opportunities and recruit them to NKU as well as conduct individual and group information sessions and provide occasional tours of campus; Assist in overall planning, leadership, and functions of the Office of Admissions. ‌ ​ ​ Manage a recruitment territory that requires developing and   maintaining   contacts with guidance counselors, schools, and organizations for the purposes of recruiting students. Significant travel included.   ​ Plan and implement assigned recruitment and yield programs.   ​ Provide pre-admissions counseling to students/families who call the office, attend an on campus or off campus event, or walk into the office .   ​ Develop and   maintain   relationships with key constituents across campus. Serve as the primary contact person for  NKU  departments and employees for questions related to visit and admission opportunities.   ​ Communicate with students and parents consistently via email, phone, text, and mail . ​   Update and run required CRM  reports   as necessary. Update student records and   assist   in assessment as needed. Update recruitment presentations and other   materials   as necessary .     KNOWLEDGE,   SKILLS   AND ABILITIES   (KSAs ): ​ ​ Ability to develop and execute comprehensive recruitment and admissions strategies to attract a diverse and talented pool of prospective students.   ​ Must have excellent interpersonal and relationship building skills .   ​ Strong analytical and   organizational   skills .   ​ Strong communication   skills and customer service skills .     EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE: ​ ​ Bachelor’s Degree   is   required .   ‌ Posted Salary: ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands: Candidate must have a valid driver's license, access to transportation, be willing to travel, and work required weekends and   evenings. ​"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Academic-Advisor_JR100333": {
      "title": "Academic Advisor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Academic Advisor ‌ Position Type: Regular ‌ About the Role: Advise undergraduate majors in the College of Informatics' Informatics Student Success Advising Center, providing academic advising, guidance and support across 13 different disciplines. The advisor will use holistic and proactive academic advising strategies towards the goal of student retention, persistence, accomplishment, and success. ‌ Advise majors and minors in the College of Informatics, including new students, current majors, and transfer students, as well as potential students. Provide personal communication with undergraduates regarding academic advising issues. Collaborate and participate in admissions, orientation, recruitment, and retention events within Academic Affairs and Student Affairs. Serve on appropriate committees (for example, Academic Advising Council). Assist the Informatics Student Success and Advising Center with special initiatives and projects. Become a Master Advisor which is an internal program to create a core of highly skilled advisors who provide high quality academic advising to support new and continuing NKU students. Attend regular training classes, conferences, and educational events to stay current on NKU policies and best practices in academic advising. Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree required. A Master’s Degree in Student Affairs, Education, College Student Personnel, or Counseling, is strongly preferred. Strong organizational and interpersonal skills, attention to detail, and exceptional communication skills are required. The ability to work with diverse populations, strong teamwork skills, and the ability to handle multiple tasks are also required. Proficiency with office software (Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook); ability to learn complex software systems (e.g. SAP and Navigate) quickly. Ability to learn, understand, and articulate the requirements, culture, and skills developed in the College of Informatics. 2 years of related experience is required preferably advising undergraduate university students. Required Documents to Upload : Resume, Cover letter, and a list of three references Position Open Until Filled. Priority review of candidates will begin September 9th. Any candidate who is offered this position will be required to undergo a pre-employment criminal background check as mandated by state law. ‌ Posted Salary: ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands: ​"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/AI-Native-Studio-Temporary-Staff_JR100360": {
      "title": "AI Native Studio Temporary Staff",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPosition Title: AI Native Studio Temporary Staff ‌ Position Type: Temporary ‌ About the Role: AI Native Studio Temporary Staff ‌ This position is intended for graduate students accepted to the AI Native Studio who have been selected to serve in a paid role. Please do not apply for this position unless you have been instructed to apply by the AI Native Studio instructor. The supervising faculty or staff member will provide the specific job responsibilities, expectations, and any additional information related to the position. ‌ Posted Salary: ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands:"
