    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Grounds-Maintenance-Temporary-Staff_JR100107": {
      "title": "Grounds/Maintenance Temporary Staff",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-03\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPosition Title: Grounds/Maintenance Temporary Staff ‌ Position Type: Temporary ‌ About the Role: Northern Kentucky University is seeking temporary staff to assist with general grounds and outdoor maintenance. This role supports campus operations through routine upkeep and seasonal tasks. ‌ Primary Responsibilities: Assist with lawn care, including mowing and trimming grass Support general outdoor maintenance and groundskeeping activities Collect and dispose of trash and debris Assist with snow and ice removal during winter months Perform other manual labor tasks as assigned Qualifications: Ability to perform physical labor in outdoor environments Willingness to work in varying weather conditions Dependable and able to follow instructions Prior grounds or maintenance experience preferred but not required ‌ Posted Salary: ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands: Ability to lift, carry, and move materials Standing, walking, bending, and working outdoors for extended periods"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/AmeriCorps-Kentucky-College-Coach_JR100241": {
      "title": "AmeriCorps Kentucky College Coach",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-31\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: AmeriCorps Kentucky College Coach ‌ Position Type: Fixed Term (Fixed Term) ‌ About the Role: The Kentucky College Coach program is an AmeriCorps program administered by Serve Kentucky and Kentucky Campus Compact and funded by AmeriCorps, the Agency. The Kentucky College Coach will work collaboratively with faculty, staff, students, and community partners to help increase the capacity for institutions to help students persist and graduate through direct mentoring/coaching/tutoring, support of high-impact practices, and/or providing service to others (on- or off-campus community service). ‌ Duration:  Full-time service, September 1, 2026 – August 31, 2027. (Service can be renewed for up to 4 terms .)     Living Allowance/Pay:   $ 1,85 0 per month in living allowance, less   FICA   and other applicable taxes   Benefits:   Healthcare and childcare eligibility, federal student loan forbearance eligibility, professional development, and an education award of up to $ 7,395 upon c ompleting service (depending on the number of months of service) for members beginning service in September . Members can also apply for SNAP, health and childcare benefits as needed, per AmeriCorps program guidelines. Minimum Qualifications :   Associate’s degree or Bachelor’s de gree (required) , excellent communication and organizational skills, and mentoring experience.    Reporting Requirements: Members are required to submit month ly activity reports to help measure impact as well as bi-weekly time sheets El igibility Requirements: Members must be at least 17 years old and a U.S. Citizen, U.S. national, or legal permanent resident alien .  Must be able to pass a National Service Criminal History Check.   ‌ Posted Salary: ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands: Members must be a U.S. Citizen, U.S. national, or legal permanent resident alien ."
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Residence-Hall-Director_JR100233": {
      "title": "Residence Hall Director",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-31\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Residence Hall Director ‌ Position Type: Fixed Term (Fixed Term) ‌ About the Role: Reporting to the Assistant Director of Residence Life, the Residence Hall Director is a 12-month live-in position responsible for coordinating all aspects of student development in the residential facilities at Northern Kentucky University. The Residence Hall Director supervises 8-18 Resident Assistants. The Residence Hall Director is responsible for staffing, training, supervising, and evaluating paraprofessional and graduate staff. ‌ ​ ​ The Residence Hall Director   is responsible for   the development and implementation of learning strategies and programming   for   residential students. This position is intended as an entry-level position for new professionals joining the Housing and Residence Life profession.   ​ This is a   contract;   an annual   12-month live-on position typically funded for up to four years.   Appointments will be made on an annual basis based on continued satisfactory performance. ​   KNOWLEDGE,   SKILLS   AND ABILITIES   (KSAs ): ​ ​ Must have excellent planning, organizational, pre sentation, programming, supervision, customer   service   and human relations skills .    Must be able to effectively communicate in both oral and written context .    Must be creative in managing   challenges   and change, able to perform under pressure, have excellent crisis management   skills,   and able to work with diverse constituents. ​     EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE: Bachelor’s   degree or higher required.     Preferred experience   includes   live-on higher education housing experience, experience mitigating crises and conflicts, experience supervising paraprofessional staff, experience with higher education student conduct, leadership skills, training in diversity/inclusion/interculturalism, and experience managing budgets . ‌ Posted Salary: ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands:"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Advisor_JR100249": {
      "title": "Advisor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-30\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Advisor ‌ Position Type: Regular ‌ About the Role: The Academic Advisor provides academic advising, guidance, and support to undergraduate students across all majors and minors within the Haile College of Business. Using a holistic and proactive advising approach, the Academic Advisor promotes student retention, persistence, achievement, and overall success. This position is part of a collaborative team of faculty and staff dedicated to student success within the Center for Student Excellence. Academic Advisors work closely with students to identify, implement, and support the most effective path to graduation, connect them with appropriate campus resources, and help them make informed academic and career decisions. Advisors build productive relationships with students, alumni, faculty, staff, and administrators across the university. Academic Advisors are expected to develop a strong understanding of the tools, systems, platforms, and organizational structures that support student success. They must maintain a thorough knowledge of university policies and demonstrate a commitment to best practices in academic advising. Members of the advising team serve as ambassadors for the Haile College of Business and are committed to collaboration, student success, creative problem-solving, and continuous professional development. ‌ Advise undergraduate students pursuing majors and minors in the Haile College of Business, including prospective, new, transfer, online, and continuing students. Communicate regularly with undergraduate students regarding academic planning, degree requirements, and other advising-related matters. Assist students in developing and achieving educational and career goals. Collaborate with campus partners and participate in admissions, orientation, recruitment, retention, and other student success initiatives within Academic Affairs and Student Affairs. Serve on university and college committees, such as the Academic Advising Council. Support the Center for Student Excellence through special initiatives, projects, and events. Complete the NKU Master Advisor Program, an internal professional development program designed to prepare advisors to provide high-quality academic advising for new and continuing students. Participate in ongoing professional development, including training, conferences, and educational opportunities, to remain current on university policies and best practices in academic advising. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Knowledge of academic advising principles, student development theory, and student success best practices, or the ability to acquire this knowledge quickly. Knowledge of university academic policies, degree requirements, curriculum, and higher education processes, or the ability to learn and apply them effectively. Strong interpersonal skills with the ability to establish trust, build relationships, and work effectively with students, faculty, staff, and diverse populations. Excellent verbal, written, and presentation communication skills. Strong organizational and time management skills with the ability to prioritize competing responsibilities, manage multiple deadlines, and maintain attention to detail. Demonstrated critical thinking, analytical, and problem-solving skills with the ability to exercise sound judgment and discretion. Ability to interpret and explain policies, procedures, and degree requirements in a clear and student-centered manner. Ability to work independently while contributing effectively within a collaborative team environment. Commitment to providing exceptional customer service and fostering an inclusive, welcoming, and supportive environment for students. Proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite (Outlook, Excel, PowerPoint, Word) and the ability to quickly learn and effectively utilize student information and advising systems such as Workday, Navigate, etc. Education and Experience: Bachelor's degree required. Master's degree in Business, Higher Education, Student Affairs, Counseling, or a related field preferred. Minimum two years of experience in academic advising, student services, higher education, or a closely related field preferred. Experience in academic advising or other relevant higher education roles is preferred; a minimum of two years is strongly preferred. Please attach a resume, cover letter and references ‌ Posted Salary: ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands: Work is performed primarily in a standard office environment.              Regular use of a computer and other office equipment is required.          Occasional evening or weekend work may be required to support orientation, recruitment, advising, and student success events. Minimal physical demands; occasional lifting of materials up to 20 pounds may be required. ​"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Director-of-Creative-Media_JR100155": {
      "title": "Director of Creative Media",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-24\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Director of Creative Media ‌ Position Type: Regular ‌ About the Role: The Director of Creative Media reports directly to the Associate Athletics Director for External Operations and serves as the lead creative professional for Athletics and is responsible for developing and producing visual content that enhances the department's brand, supports recruiting efforts, engages fans and promotes the success of NKU student-athletes and programs. Working closely with coaches, student-athletes, athletics administrators and external operations staff, the Director of Creative Media develops and executes content strategies across digital and social media platforms through photography, videography, graphic design and other multimedia storytelling. The position plays a key role in advancing departmental priorities related to fan engagement, recruiting, ticket sales, fundraising and brand awareness. The Director of Creative Media provides creative leadership for athletics content production while also serving as a hands-on content creator. The position manages student workers and interns, establishes creative standards and helps ensure a consistent and recognizable visual identity for NKU Athletics. Compliance with NCAA rules is of the utmost importance at Northern Kentucky University. As a member of the athletics department staff, it is expected that the Director of Creative Media will have a full understanding of the NCAA rules that pertain to the position. It is also expected that the Director of Creative Media will comply with all NCAA rules and if he/she becomes aware, or have reasonable cause to believe, that a violation of a rule has occurred he/she will immediately report it to the Director of Athletics or his/her designee. ‌ Creative Content Development and Storytelling Lead the planning, creation and production of multimedia content that promotes NKU Athletics, supports recruiting efforts, enhances fan engagement and highlights the achievements of student-athletes, coaches and programs. Produce content for social media, digital platforms, athletics websites, recruiting materials, fundraising initiatives and special projects. Photography, Videography and Graphic Design Serve as the department's primary visual content creator through photography, videography and graphic design. Capture athletics events, practices, community engagement activities and special events while producing creative assets that support departmental initiatives. Content Strategy and Brand Management Develop content plans and creative strategies that align with departmental goals and maintain a consistent visual identity across athletics platforms. Collaborate with athletics leadership and external operations staff to identify storytelling opportunities and support strategic priorities. Collaboration and Project Support Work closely with coaches, student-athletes, athletics communications, marketing, ticketing, development and corporate partnerships staff to create content that supports recruiting, fan engagement, sponsorship fulfillment and revenue-generating initiatives. Student Staff Supervision and Creative Operations Recruit, train and supervise student employees and interns. Assist with content scheduling, asset organization, equipment management and workflow coordination to support departmental creative needs. Knowledge Skills & Abilities Demonstrated experience in photography, videography & graphic design. Proficiency with Adobe Creative Cloud, including Photoshop, Illustrator, Premier Pro & related applications. Strong visual storytelling, creative thinking and content development skills. Knowledge of social media content creation and digital communication platforms. Ability to manage multiple projects and meet deadlines in a fast-paced environment. Strong communication, collaboration and organizational skills. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in Communications, Digital Media, Graphic Design, Marketing, Journalism, Photography, Video Production or a related field. Preferred Qualifications: Experience working in NCAA athletics, supervising student employees or interns, experience with motion graphics, animation or advanced video production techniques and a portfolio demonstrating photography, videography and graphic design work. Experience: Minimum of three years of professional experience in multimedia production, creative media, digital content creation, athletics communications, marketing or a related field. Preferred experience in collegiate athletics, professional sports or a comparable environment. ‌ Posted Salary: ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands: Ability to work evenings, weekends, some holidays and limited travel as required. Must have a valid driver’s license."
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Part-time-Faculty--First-Year-Composition-and-Reading_JR100234": {
      "title": "Part-time Faculty, First-Year Composition and Reading",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-22\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPosition Title: Part-time Faculty, First-Year Composition and Reading ‌ Position Type: Fixed Term (Fixed Term) ‌ About the Role: The Writing Instruction Program (housed in the Department of English) is seeking part-time adjunct faculty. Faculty members might teach first-year writing or reading courses, including co-requisite courses with reading or writing support, and reading. These positions report to the Director of the Writing instruction Program. ‌ Teach between three and nine hours (1-3 classes) of college writing and/or reading per semester. Provide support to students through office hours. Align assignments and curriculum with programmatic and university student learning outcomes. Master’s Degree in English or a closely related field (with at least 18 hours of graduate coursework in English) Strong background in and evidence of teaching composition and reading and working with first-year students. Experience teaching co-requisite writing courses and/or experience teaching non-native speakers is desired, as is a commitment to intercultural competence and inclusive excellence. The pay for a three-credit varies slightly based on years of experience and education but is projected to be between $2700 and $3000 per three-credit course. In addition, the position is designed for candidates planning to seek permanent positions elsewhere. The department will provide mentoring and performance reviews as well as support for continuing job searches. Required Documents Curriculum Vitae References Scholarly Work Evidence of teaching style and effectiveness Teaching Philosophy ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands:"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Part-Time-Faculty---Mechanical--Manufacturing--Mechatronics--Electrical-or-Electronics_JR100235": {
      "title": "Part-Time Faculty - Mechanical, Manufacturing, Mechatronics, Electrical or Electronics",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-22\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPosition Title: Part-Time Faculty - Mechanical, Manufacturing, Mechatronics, Electrical or Electronics ‌ Position Type: Fixed Term (Fixed Term) ‌ About the Role: The Department of Physics, Geology, and Engineering Technology seeks to create a database of potential part-time instructors who are qualified to teach courses in engineering technology. Note that there is not a specific position associated with this posting. ‌ Teaching responsibilities include For labs: Creating a syllabus and schedule of labs in consultation with the course coordinator and lecture instructor Setting up lab equipment before and taking it down after each class Supervising and guiding students during class Grading work turned in by students Entering grades in the Canvas learning management system.   For lectures: Creating a syllabus and schedule that matches the course description and satisfies learning objectives in consultation with the course coordinator, if applicable, and program director Working with lab instructors to set schedule of lab exercises, grading expectations, etc., if applicable, Holding classes as scheduled Assigning and grading homework Writing and grading exams Using the Canvas learning management system Reporting attendance and submitting mid-term and final grades on time.   For both: being available one hour per week outside of the scheduled course meeting time to answer student questions. Candidates must meet the following minimum educational qualifications: (1) Master’s degree (2) At least 18 credit-hours graduate coursework in engineering, in engineering technology, or in a related field or equivalent in work experience. Required Documents: Cover letter/letter of application Curriculum Vitae Names and contact information of 2-3 professional references ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands:"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Part-time-Instructor-in-Art---Design-Foundations_JR100229": {
      "title": "Part-time Instructor in Art & Design Foundations",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-21\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPosition Title: Part-time Instructor in Art & Design Foundations ‌ Position Type: Fixed Term (Fixed Term) ‌ About the Role: The Art & Design program in the School of the Arts (SOTA) at Northern Kentucky University (NKU) invites applications for its ongoing pool of part-time instructors to teach in our Foundations program. We are seeking a passionate and skilled artist-educator to teach foundational studio courses in Art & Design. The ideal candidate will have a strong background in traditional and contemporary visual practices and a commitment to developing students’ creative and conceptual abilities in the early stages of their academic journey. While there is no specific position associated with this posting at this time, applications will be used to build a qualified database of instructors for future instructional needs. ABOUT SOTA The Art & Design, Music, and Theatre & Dance programs make up the School of the Arts which sits in the College of Arts and Sciences at Northern Kentucky University. Art & Design offers an innovative and engaged opportunity for aspiring artists and designers who seek professional training in the arts. Art & Design has 17 full-time faculty and 4 full-time staff that embrace a comprehensive hands-on approach of working with materials and techniques while developing critical thinking skills related to the various art disciplines and studio training. ABOUT NKU Established in 1968, NKU is a 15,000-student, nationally recognized, growing metropolitan university located seven miles from downtown Cincinnati, Ohio. Greater Cincinnati has one of the most vibrant and multifaceted cultural scenes in the Midwest, with the Cincinnati Art Museum, Contemporary Arts Center, 21c Museum Hotel and a plethora of galleries such as The Weston, Carl Solway and Manifest Gallery. Cincinnati offers an outstanding quality of life, a dynamic arts community, and an affordable cost of living. NKU is committed to active engagement with the Northern Kentucky/Greater Cincinnati region of over two million people. ‌ The primary responsibilities of this position are to teach courses at the foundational levels   ART   130 Creating Visual Form,   ART   135 Creating Visual Order or other studio disciplines, depending on departmental needs and the candidate’s qualifications. Additionally, to maintain and work within the set curriculum of our course offerings as we encourage exploration of diverse topics and collaboration across the campus and region. Deliver engaging, instruction aligned with departmental learning outcomes. Foster student understanding of form, space, time and composition through observational and media-based work. Teach basic fabrication techniques, color theory and material exploration. Guide students in developing critical thinking, visual literacy and problem-solving skills. Introduce students to historical and contemporary artists/designers, and encourage exploration of cultural, ethical, and social dimensions of art. Support student development in research, writing, and speaking about art and design. Maintain a positive, collaborative classroom and studio environment. Additional responsibilities include some student mentoring, responsible studio management, and provide direction and guidance for advancing the University’s strategic priorities. The foundations studios are equipped with Mac instructor stations, smart technology, and ample student workspace. The drawing studio ( FAC   415) is located in the Fine Arts Center that includes state of the art lighting, natural north lit ceiling windows, ample room space, drawing chair/desks, figure model stand, large still life closet, and overhead screen and projector.   Join a community of dedicated educators and working artists who are shaping the next generation of creative thinkers. Submit your application to be considered for upcoming part-time instructional opportunities. Minimum qualifications include an   MFA   in Visual Arts or Design or its equivalent, an active professional creative practice, a demonstrated knowledge of drawing techniques, and well versed in contemporary / historical practice. Demonstrated commitment and/or experience promoting and fostering a positive learning environment. The position includes possible opportunities to shape curricula and be part of a team of committed colleagues and dedicated students. College-level teaching experience preferred. Applicants should clearly demonstrate strengths and technical experience in the afore-mentioned areas of expertise. To apply, submit the following items electronically: Cover Letter (outlining qualifications) CV Names and Contact Information of 3 references Artist Statement / Research Interests Portfolio of Professional Work  (20 images of personal work with descriptions/image list) Teaching Philosophy Portfolio of Student Work (20 images of student work with descriptions/image list) ** Portfolio of Professional Work and Portfolio of Student Work may either be a link to a website or submit a   PDF   attachment   Questions regarding the nature of the position should be directed to Julia Sebastian, Foundations Coordinator, via email:   sebastianj4@nku.edu   Applications will be used to create a database of potential instructors. ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands:"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Political-Science--Criminal-Justice--Organizational-Leadership--Law--International-Studies--and-Public-Administration-Adjunct-Faculty-Applicant-Pool_JR100197": {
      "title": "Political Science, Criminal Justice, Organizational Leadership, Law, International Studies, and Public Administration Adjunct Faculty Applicant Pool",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-20\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPosition Title: Political Science, Criminal Justice, Organizational Leadership, Law, International Studies, and Public Administration Adjunct Faculty Applicant Pool ‌ Position Type: Fixed Term (Fixed Term) ‌ About the Role: The Department of Political Science, Criminal Justice, and Organizational Leadership at Northern Kentucky University is seeking to create a database of potential part-time instructors who are qualified to teach courses in one or more of the following disciplines: Political Science, Criminal Justice, and Organizational Leadership. THERE IS NOT A SPECIFIC POSITION ASSOCIATED WITH THIS POSTING. THIS POSTING WILL BE USED TO CREATE A DATABASE OF POTENTIAL PART-TIME FACULTY. ‌ Teaching responsibilities involve:  1) Teaching a three-credit hour course.  2) Creating a syllabus with a timeline of classes for students.  3) Provide a meeting time for students.  4) Managing the MyNKU online grading system.    Also, under the direction of the Academic Department Chair:  Develop and manage syllabus materials. The adjunct professor is responsible for selecting and compiling tests, assignments and/or online discussion exercises that permit measurement of performance relative to standardized learning objectives.    Coordinate courseware and curriculum with academic department chair. The adjunct professor is responsible for reviewing any textbook and other courseware changes with the academic department chair and other full-time faculty teaching the course.    Facilitate class instruction. The adjunct professor is responsible for teaching the assigned class in accordance with learning objectives and session plan outlines    The adjunct professor is expected to administer evaluations of student performance based on course deliverables and course rubrics.    All course grades must be posted in MyNKU. Qualifications: All applicants must have a minimum of a Master’s Degree in one of the following disciplines: Political Science, Criminal Justice, Organizational Leadership, Public Administration (or related fields).    Please submit your application with a cover letter, vitae, transcripts, and the names of at least three professional references   Any candidate selected for this position will be required to undergo a pre-employment criminal background check as mandated by state law. ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands:"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Nursing--MSN-Program--Part-time-Faculty_JR100210": {
      "title": "Nursing (MSN Program) Part-time Faculty",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-15\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPosition Title: Nursing (MSN Program) Part-time Faculty ‌ Position Type: Fixed Term (Fixed Term) ‌ About the Role: The Department of Nursing invites applications for online adjunct faculty positions for the CCNE accredited MSN program. ‌ Faculty responsibilities will include teaching in online didactic courses. Courses run in 7-week sessions. Faculty may teach in the core MSN courses as well as the specialty courses within the MSN tracks based upon degree and experience. Tracks in the MSN program include : Family Nurse Practitioner Adult Gerontology Acute Care Nurse Practitioner Psych/Mental Health Nurse Practitioner Nurse Executive Leader Nurse Educator Timeline: The search will remain open indefinitely as needs vary semester to semester. Qualifications : Doctorate required Teaching experience in nursing desirable. Experience related to specific tracks within the MSN program is necessary. Must possess a valid nursing license in the state of residence. A valid, unencumbered Advanced Practice Nurse Practitioner license in the state of residence is required to teach in the nurse practitioner tracks. Advanced Practice Nurse Practitioner applicants must be board-certified in their specialty area. ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands:"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Annual-Giving-Officer--Athletics_JR100209": {
      "title": "Annual Giving Officer, Athletics",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-15\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Annual Giving Officer, Athletics ‌ Position Type: Regular ‌ About the Role: Implement strategic fundraising initiatives for the Division of Athletics by soliciting philanthropic commitments, coordinating targeted appeals, supporting sport-specific crowdfunding campaigns, and leading all Go Norse Fund efforts in close collaboration with several key teams across Athletics and Advancement. ‌ Manage and implement strategic efforts to strengthen philanthropic support for the Division of Athletics, including soliciting annual gifts—typically ranging from $1,000 to $25,000—coordinating targeted appeals, and supporting sport-specific crowdfunding campaigns. Coordinate and execute all Go Norse Fund initiatives, working closely with colleagues in annual giving, alumni communications, donor engagement, and athletics ticketing to increase donor participation, implement effective stewardship plans, and enhance alumni affinity to Norse athletics. Document and maintain quality records in the donor database (Raiser’s Edge   NXT ) adhering to all established reporting deadlines, utilizing university systems to record prospect and donor interactions, track proposals, and maintain prospect and donor contact information. Manage special projects and development functions assigned by the Associate Athletic Director for Development, including communication to external stakeholders and internal partners, donor and prospect events, sport-specific alumni events and receptions, and volunteer engagement opportunities. Qualifications Bachelor’s degree and 2 years of related experience required. The successful candidate will demonstrate a positive growth mindset and a passion for higher education and collegiate athletics. Candidates should have a foundational understanding of fundraising principles. Proficiency with Microsoft Windows applications, including Teams, is required, and familiarity with Raiser’s Edge is preferred. Strong communication skills and the ability to work independently are essential. Please attach resume, cover letter and references. ‌ Posted Salary: ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands:"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Standard-Patient-Actor_JR100173": {
